ied. node1's installed curl version was preserved and placed in a persistent APT/dpkg hold. The mandatory restart protocol was also completed coherently, and curl recovered installed, executable, held, and at the original version. Operational hygiene was clean.","limitations":["No actual system-update transaction was captured. The conclusion that a future update will leave curl unchanged rests on the directly verified APT/dpkg hold state, which is the package manager's native mechanism for this outcome."]}
